  "executive_briefing": "The 2026 tax landscape is defined by the hardening of administrative compliance and the stabilization of new trade paradigms. The US-centric Section 232 tariff framework has matured from an emergency measure into a foundational tool for industrial policy, characterized by assertive judicial support for retroactive reliquidation. Globally, Pillar Two has transitioned from an aspirational policy into the 'Fatigue' phase of routine operational compliance for multinational enterprises. In the APAC region, particularly Singapore, digital tax compliance has accelerated, with the integration of real-time e-invoicing (InvoiceNow) becoming a non-negotiable standard for GST auditability. Meanwhile, the emerging dialogue around AI-induced tax base erosion indicates an early shift toward structural alternatives to traditional labor-based taxation.",
